# tools/d/declared_model_witness.rish -- one model and one configured effort, each named once
# and agreed everywhere the tree describes it.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. On 20260824 Keaton asked to return this clone to Opus 5 and found the tree already
# disagreed with itself about which model it ran. `.claude/settings.json` and
# GLOW_PROFILE.template.kyri read claude-opus-5; recursion-prompts/seed/autonomous-loop.seed.md read
# claude-opus-4-6; and the personal GLOW_PROFILE.kyri carried claude-opus-4-6 in its field directly
# beneath a comment of its own that said `Model is Opus 5`. A file disagreeing with itself is the
# clearest form the fault takes, and nothing in the tree could see any of it. REDS %201.
#
# This is the fifth time this shape has been booked -- REDS %187, %190, %192, %199 -- so it stops
# being a habit and becomes a reading: tools/fixtures/d/declared_model.sh answers the question once,
# from .claude/settings.json, the file that actually drives which model Claude Code loads. A
# description agrees with the thing it describes, so the driver is the source.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN, on metal.
#   Every site on the declaring roster names the model the driver names. Three stand there as of
#   20260824.161948: the profile template a fresh clone copies, the autonomous-loop seed an
#   unattended run reads, and the session-logs law that tells a log what to record.
#   Twenty-six behaviors on real git repositories in a throwaway pen, every refusal shown from both
#   sides: agreement free, a stale site bitten and counted, an absent site bitten, a page recounting
#   old models beside the current one free, dated testimony free by basename and by date/ room, a
#   living drifted file counted, the ratchet ceiling proven from both sides, `claude-code` and
#   `.claude-state` read as the ordinary words they are, the reading refusing rather than defaulting
#   twice over, and the reading anchored to its own location rather than the caller's cwd.
#
#   AND THE EFFORT ROSTER, seated 20260916. This scan read `effortLevel` from the same driver on
#   every run since it was written, printed `declared_effort=`, and compared it with nothing -- so
#   the one field it measured and never gated is the one that drifted. `.claude/rules/session-logs.md`
#   said the file configured `max` while the file read `medium`, its own peer
#   `.claude/rules/session-log-provenance.md` said `medium` correctly the whole time, and the seed's
#   section 0 and this family's own USAGE comment said `max` beside them. Two law pages disagreed
#   about one tracked file and nothing in the tree could hear it.
#
#   THE EFFORT IS NOT ONE VALUE, and the roster is shaped around that. `tools/f/fleet_lap.sh` execs
#   `--effort max` inside the enclosure while `tools/f/fleet-loop.sh` execs `--effort medium` bare,
#   which this pier runs, so a page describing a LAUNCH PATH is right to write either word. Four
#   pages state what `.claude/settings.json` ITSELF carries and those four are gated, by presence of
#   the driver's value -- the same presence-over-absence discipline the model half keeps, so a page
#   teaching the split stays free to name both efforts in one sentence. Ten further behaviors prove
#   it: the reading reported, the roster counted, agreement free, a stale site bitten and counted,
#   the two gates told apart, an absent roster path bitten, the launch-path sentence free, the
#   driver proven to be the source, and the whole roster reddening together when the driver moves.
#
#   THE CONTROL NOW ANSWERS FOR ITS OWN LEGS. Every reading prints through one `leg` function that
#   tallies it, and `control_verdict` reads `leg_failed` when any leg does. Until this stamp a `no`
#   stood beneath a green `control_verdict=ok` unless the witness happened to name that key, so a
#   leg written tomorrow was unheard until somebody remembered to assert it. Both mutations planted
#   on the seating lap were caught at the verdict rather than at a named key: dropping `effort_over`
#   from the gate, and reading a baked `max` in place of the driver's value.
#
# WHAT IS REPORTED, as a ratchet under a ceiling that only ever falls. Living tracked files naming
# some model id and never the current one -- one at seating, a lineage page recording the model that
# generated it. Honest testimony wearing no stamp, which only a reader can tell from real drift.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. That the model named is the model the API actually served. This reads what the
# tree says about itself, and agreement is the whole of the claim.
#
# Style: context/GAUGE_STYLE.md - Rule: .claude/rules/session-logs.md
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/d/declared_model_witness.rish

say "declared-model: Language EN -- a constant spelled four ways is a constant that can disagree with itself."
say "declared-model: Style Gauge -- the driver is the reading, and every description agrees with it."
say "declared-model: Lens TAME -- say why, once, in one place, and let the rest of the tree cite it."

let scan = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/d/declared_model_scan.sh"]
say scan.out
assert scan.ok else "declared-model: a site that states which model this clone runs disagrees with the driver"
assert scan.out contains "declaring_over=0" else "declared-model: every declaring site must name the model the driver names"
assert scan.out contains "declaring_effort_over=0" else "declared-model: every page stating what .claude/settings.json carries must name the effort the driver names"
assert scan.out contains "verdict=ok" else "declared-model: the scan must balance before it is believed"
say "field GREEN -- one model and one configured effort, agreed everywhere they are described"

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/d/declared_model_control.sh"]
say control.out
assert control.ok else "declared-model: the control must complete"
assert control.out contains "agreement_free=yes" else "declared-model: a tree whose sites agree must pass free"
assert control.out contains "reading_reported=yes" else "declared-model: the scan must print the reading it measured against"
assert control.out contains "stale_site_bitten=yes" else "declared-model: a declaring site naming another model must red"
assert control.out contains "stale_site_counted=yes" else "declared-model: the count must name how many sites disagreed"
assert control.out contains "absent_site_bitten=yes" else "declared-model: a roster path that has gone missing must red rather than be skipped"
assert control.out contains "history_free=yes" else "declared-model: a page recounting old models beside the current one must pass free"
assert control.out contains "dated_free=yes" else "declared-model: dated testimony keeps every word it wrote"
assert control.out contains "dated_verdict_ok=yes" else "declared-model: dated testimony must leave the verdict green"
assert control.out contains "living_drift_counted=yes" else "declared-model: a living file naming another model must be counted"
assert control.out contains "at_ceiling_free=yes" else "declared-model: the ratchet must pass at its ceiling"
assert control.out contains "over_ceiling_counted=yes" else "declared-model: the ratchet must count what stands above it"
assert control.out contains "over_ceiling_bitten=yes" else "declared-model: one above the ceiling must red, so no override exists"
assert control.out contains "claude_word_free=yes" else "declared-model: claude-code and .claude-state are ordinary words, never model ids"
assert control.out contains "absent_settings_refused=yes" else "declared-model: an unreadable driver must refuse rather than default"
assert control.out contains "missing_key_refused=yes" else "declared-model: a driver naming no model must refuse rather than default"
assert control.out contains "reading_root_anchored=yes" else "declared-model: the reading resolves from its own location, never the caller's cwd"
assert control.out contains "effort_reading_reported=yes" else "declared-model: the scan must print the effort it measured against"
assert control.out contains "effort_agreement_free=yes" else "declared-model: an effort roster in agreement must pass free"
assert control.out contains "effort_roster_counted=yes" else "declared-model: the count must name how many pages state the settings effort"
assert control.out contains "effort_stale_bitten=yes" else "declared-model: a page naming an effort the driver does not carry must red"
assert control.out contains "effort_stale_counted=yes" else "declared-model: the count must name how many effort pages disagreed"
assert control.out contains "effort_gate_independent=yes" else "declared-model: the model gate and the effort gate must be told apart"
assert control.out contains "effort_absent_bitten=yes" else "declared-model: an effort roster path that has gone missing must red rather than be skipped"
assert control.out contains "effort_launch_path_free=yes" else "declared-model: a page naming a launch path's own effort beside the settings value must pass free"
assert control.out contains "effort_driver_is_source=yes" else "declared-model: the effort gate must read the driver rather than a baked value"
assert control.out contains "effort_whole_roster_bitten=yes" else "declared-model: a driver that moves must carry its whole roster with it"
assert control.out contains "control_failed=0" else "declared-model: every leg the control prints must pass, including one written after this line"
assert control.out contains "control_verdict=ok" else "declared-model: the control must agree with itself"
say "thirty-seven behaviors proven on real git repositories, every refusal shown from both sides -- and the local override read apart from the tracked default, gated on neither"

say "GREEN: declared-model -- one model and one configured effort, each named once and agreed everywhere it is described."
